      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-275500",
      ":question/problem": "A point is chosen uniformly at random from the interval $[0,1].$ Let the continuous random variable $X$ be the distance from the origin to the chosen point. Consider the triangle with vertices at $(0,0),(1,0),$ and $(1,X).$ Let $A=A(X)$ denote the area of this triangle. \n\nExpressing the integrand in the following equation as a polynomial, we have\n\n$\\text{E}[A]={\\int }_{0}^{1}$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{d}x.$\n\nTherefore, the expected area of the triangle is \n{{field-2}}."
