      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-275499",
      ":question/problem": "A stick of length $1$ is broken at a point chosen uniformly at random along its length. Let the continuous random variable $X$ denote the distance from the left end of the stick to the break point, and let $Y=Y(X)$ denote the length of the longest piece.\n\nExpressing the integrands in the following equation as polynomials, we have\n\n$\\text{E}[Y]={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\text{d}x.$\n\nTherefore, the expected length of the longer piece is \n{{field-3}}."
